            "id": "4946561",
            "title": "AVLV: Exploring Value In The U.S. Large Cap Universe",
            "description": "<html><body><figure class=\"getty-figure\" data-type=\"getty-image\"><picture> <img alt=\"Business Value Added Concept. Businessperson touching slider moving from minimum to maximum, value increase, service enhancement, company value added, add mindset, and strategic business growth.\" data-id=\"2223416632\" data-type=\"getty-image\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"988\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 132px), (max-width: 1199px) calc(100vw - 666px), (max-width: 1307px) calc(100vw - 708px), 600px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w630\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w1536 1536w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w1280 1280w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w1080 1080w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w750 750w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w640 640w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w480 480w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w320 320w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2223416632/image_2223416632.jpg?io=getty-c-w240 240w\" width=\"1536\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p> <p class=\"item-credits\">Sandwish/iStock via Getty Images</p></figcaption></figure><p data-eci=\"true\">American Century Investments-backed Avantis Investors has a wide range of low-cost thematic ETFs that could potentially fit anyone's portfolio, and the one we're going to learn about today is the Avantis U.S. Large Cap Value ETF (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AVLV\" title=\"Avantis US Large Cap Value ETF\">AVLV</a></span>). I won't be analyzing it from an investing point of view, though. This article is a primer on this $22 billion fund that's been around, coming up on five years from September 21, 2021, and it's meant to familiarize you with how the ETF is constructed, what it's delivered so far, and what its long-term prospects look like.</p> <h2>What Is AVLV?</h2> <p>The ETF is focused on a <a href=\"https://www.avantisinvestors.com/avantis-investments/avantis-us-large-cap-value-etf/#overview\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.avantisinvestors.com/avantis-investments/avantis-us-large-cap-value-etf/#overview\">single outcome</a>, and that's long-term capital appreciation. You've probably figured out from the name that it tracks some value benchmark, and you're right. It's the Russell 1000 Value Index. You'll notice that the fund tracks the index pretty closely with its <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AVLV/risk\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AVLV/risk\">sub-2%</a> tracking error and 7% annual turnover, but it only holds about 300 stocks.</p> <p>The reason that's much fewer than what the index holds is the ETF's selection method. The index's constituents are put through a couple of filtration steps that involve profitability ratios and valuations. The ETF specifically looks at book to market value and profits to book value. Book value is just shareholder equity, so the ETF's sights are set on companies in the U.S. large-cap camp that are trading at discounts to equity and pre-tax earnings per dollar of book value.</p> <p>That's the gist of what the ETF looks for, and that's built on top of <a href=\"https://www.lseg.com/en/ftse-russell/indices/russell-us-style\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.lseg.com/en/ftse-russell/indices/russell-us-style\">what the index looks for</a>, with some differences:</p> <blockquote><p>The index includes companies with relatively lower price to-book ratios, lower 2-year I/B/E/S forecast growth and lower historical 5-year sales growth. The index is reconstituted fully in June to ensure accurate representation of the US large cap value style, with updates for parent index membership changes in December and quarterly IPO inclusions in March and September. Since March 24, 2025, the index applies quarterly capping if constituent weights exceed target RIC thresholds. IPOs with investable market cap above the Russell Top 500 breakpoint are eligible for fast entry; breakpoints are set semi-annually and market-adjusted quarterly.</p></blockquote> <p>The ETF takes the whole index and applies its own valuation formulas to get to the final list of ~300 stocks. You're getting all of this in one basket at an expense ratio of 0.15%. There's a nominal yield of 1% that should more than cover the fees, if that's how you're thinking about it.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure a-c\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <img alt=\"Avantis Investors\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"722\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890045184718544.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890045184718544.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890045184718544.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890045184718544.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"553\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Avantis Investors</span></p></figcaption></figure><p>The holdings are pretty diverse, but what you want to do is make note of the top sectors. Financials, consumer discretionary, and energy make up more than half the ETF's assets, and that's something you always want to be aware of because a shift in the mix could mean completely different results.</p> <h2>Performance Since 2021</h2> <p>The ETF has done better than the benchmark, so the strategy it's been using definitely works. Or has worked. The last three years have been pretty good for the ETF.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure a-c\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"334\" data-og-image-facebook=\"false\" data-og-image-google_news=\"false\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"false\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"false\" data-og-image-msn=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"false\" data-width=\"1793\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/7/59285166-17887914714713182_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"Avantis Investors\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"119\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/7/59285166-17887914714713182_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/7/59285166-17887914714713182_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/7/59285166-17887914714713182_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/7/59285166-17887914714713182_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/7/59285166-17887914714713182_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Avantis Investors</span></p></figcaption></figure><p>We've got benchmark-beating performance, and that little bit of alpha being wrung out of the portfolio is a good sign that fund managers are working with a strategy that's proven itself over the AI supercycle we're in. We'll see what that looks like with the dividends reinvested, but let's also look at how AVLV's done against a pure Russell 1000 Value Index holding, which is what the iShares Russell 1000 Value ETF (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/IWD\" title=\"iShares Russell 1000 Value ETF\">IWD</a>) is. I've also roped in Vanguard's Russell 1000 Value ETF (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VONV\" title=\"Vanguard Russell 1000 Value ETF\">VONV</a>).</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure a-c\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"623\" data-og-image-facebook=\"true\" data-og-image-google_news=\"true\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"true\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"true\" data-og-image-msn=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"true\" data-width=\"1723\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-17888723343417907_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"SA\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"231\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-17888723343417907_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-17888723343417907_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-17888723343417907_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-17888723343417907_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-17888723343417907_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>SA</span></p></figcaption></figure><p>I'll leave you to mull over that, because what I'd really like to get into is how this ETF is positioned going forward.</p> <p>If you're looking at the decade ahead, I think value stocks rotating into prominence over the past year is a sign from the market that it can't absorb that much risk. You can see growth stocks (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/IWF\" title=\"iShares Russell 1000 Growth ETF\">IWF</a>) running flat, but value stocks (IWD) don't look like they saw the stop sign.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure a-c\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"627\" data-og-image-facebook=\"true\" data-og-image-google_news=\"true\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"true\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"true\" data-og-image-msn=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"true\" data-width=\"1728\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-1788875952052727_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"SA\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"232\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-1788875952052727_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-1788875952052727_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-1788875952052727_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-1788875952052727_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/8/59285166-1788875952052727_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>SA</span></p></figcaption></figure><p>These are just signs. You're free to read them as you like. I'm just saying that an ETF with a value strategy could do well in the next decade. It's up to you to decide if it can or can't.</p> <h2>Summary</h2> <p>The ETF follows a strategy that's allowed it to beat the benchmark and other indexes over a 5-year period, and the risk seems to be lower than owning a broad, unfiltered set of large caps. The balance between pros and cons seems even. It's got a good grip on risk and value, and it's shown its shareholders that the methodology works. It's also a cheap way to have your portfolio risk managed by professionals.</p> <p>I'm hoping this gives you a good springboard for your decision on AVLV. Be sure to look at the macro picture with as much objectivity as you can because good news on employment or a slowdown in inflation won't be that great for a value ETF. The market narrative can and will change based on economic developments, and having a balanced portfolio can be crucial when the narrative changes. For AVLV, the best counterfoil would be a growth fund.</p> <p>Avantis has a couple of mutual funds (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/TNRAX\" title=\"1290 Avantis US Large Cap Growth Fund; A\">TNRAX</a>) (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/TNXIX\" title=\"1290 Avantis US Large Cap Growth Fund; I\">TNXIX</a>) that focus on the same market cap segment, and we're seeing these underperform the market as AVLV zooms ahead.</p> <figure class=\"regular-img-figure a-c\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"629\" data-og-image-facebook=\"true\" data-og-image-google_news=\"true\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"true\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"true\" data-og-image-msn=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"true\" data-width=\"1742\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890033819442487_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"SA\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"231\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890033819442487_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890033819442487_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890033819442487_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890033819442487_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/9/59285166-17890033819442487_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>SA</span></p></figcaption></figure><p>It's always a good idea to look for balanced opportunities when you're facing a macro environment that could go either way. With AVLV focused on value, there could be opportunities to balance your portfolio with a growth-focused fund and adjust the weightings based on the environment changes.</p> <p>This article answers three questions about AVLV:</p> <ul> <li>What is the best way for AVLV to work in a portfolio?</li> <li>How is AVLV's portfolio constructed, and how are its sector allocation weightings?</li> <li>How has AVLV performed against its benchmark in different investing environments?</li> </ul> <div class=\"R6FbO flex sa-text-content sa-media-content sa-table-content sa-content-helpers print:block mb-32\"><div class=\"w-0 grow print:w-auto\"><div><div class=\"T2G6W\" data-test-id=\"content-container\"><p class=\"paywall-full-content\"><span><em>Editor's note:</em></span><em> This article is intended to provide a general overview of the ETF for educational purposes only and, unlike other articles on Seeking Alpha, does not offer an investment opinion about the ETF.</em></p></div></div></div></div> </body></html>",
